  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Trust is important to any effective partnership. It allows us to be candid, supportive, and willing to take risks with each other. The goal is to build trust on your team by starting with yourself.\n\n[Building Trust](video \"LiL3_Building_Trust\")\n\n**Watch**: *Building Trust*\n\n---\n\n### Self-assessment\n\nTake 30 minutes this week to think about your strengths and weaknesses regarding trust. Use this [Trust Self-Assessment](Glint_Manager_Trust_Self-Assessment) to create a summary of your current status and goals for improvement.\n\nThen seek candid advice from someone you trust at work on your assessment of yourself and on your proposed goals.\n\n### Ask your team for feedback\n\nShare your self-assessment and proposed solutions with your team. Ask them to help you select your single most important improvement goal.\n\n### Commit to one thing\n\nOnce you've determined your most important goal, set achievable and measurable milestones that will help you achieve it. Seek feedback along the way from your team and others you trust.",
